{% set steps = [
    "Exploring materials and technologies",
    "Experimenting with tools and processes",
    "Developing ideas through prototyping",
    "Learning from both successes and failures",
] %}
<section class="about-methodology">
    <div class="about-methodology-inner">
        <div class="about-methodology-intro">
            <div class="about-methodology-main">
                <h2 class="about-methodology-title">What is the Learning methodology behind?</h2>
                <p class="about-methodology-lead">
                    The Learning Hub is grounded in a participatory, community-based and practice-oriented approach to learning, with learning through making at its core.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="about-methodology-aside">
                <p>
                    Drawing on Fab Lab Barcelona's experience in collaborative research, digital fabrication and open education, it understands learning as an active process built through experimentation, hands-on practice, knowledge exchange and collaboration.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Rather than following a one-size-fits-all learning pathway, the methodology starts from the knowledge, skills and experiences already present within communities. <strong>It encourages people to learn by doing:</strong>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="about-methodology-steps">
            {% for step in steps %}
                <li class="about-methodology-step">
                    <span class="about-methodology-step-number">{{ "%02d" % loop.index }}</span>
                    <p class="about-methodology-step-text">{{ step }}</p>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>
        <p class="about-methodology-statement">
            Understanding the practice of <em>making</em> a way to question, develop skills and transform ideas into practice.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
